1 dup . .
1 2 swap . .
1 2 over . . .
1 2 3 rot . . .
99 88 drop .s

clear
: dup-via-rs >r r@ r> ;
7 dup-via-rs . .
: store-fetch >r r> ;
42 store-fetch .
: peek-twice >r r@ r@ r> ;
9 peek-twice . . .

clear
1 2 nip . cr

\ pick copies the nth item from the top, leaving it in place; roll moves it
1 2 3 0 pick .s cr              \ 1 2 3 3
clear
1 2 3 1 pick .s cr              \ 1 2 3 2
clear
1 2 3 2 pick .s cr              \ 1 2 3 1
clear
1 2 3 2 roll .s cr              \ 2 3 1 — moved, not copied
clear
[ 100 200 300 ] [ 2 0 ] [: 2 pick swap @i :] map . cr   \ [ 300 100 ] — the array is reached below map's source
drop
\ !at is pick's write counterpart: n counts from the value being stored
1 2 3  99 2 !at .s cr           \ 1 99 3 — the item 2 deep (counting from 99) is overwritten
clear
1 2 3  99 1 !at .s cr           \ 1 2 99
clear
10 20  5  2 pick f+ 2 !at  drop .s cr   \ 15 — read, add, store: one fused op, then 20 dropped
clear
[ 10 20 30 ] [ 2 0 ] 0 [: 3 pick 1 pick @i  2 pick f+ 2 !at  drop :] reduce . cr  \ 40   30 + 10
clear

1 2 3 3 pick                    \ (depth 3 with only 3 values below the count)
clear
1 2 -1 pick                     \ (negative depth)
clear
1 2  9 5 !at                    \ (store depth past the stack)
clear
1 2  9 0 !at                    \ (depth 0 would store onto the value itself)
clear
5 >side side-peek . side-depth . side-drop cr
